            <div xml:id="m-8189c447-e6dc-4725-b4df-286f0beefb6d">
              <lg xml:id="m-0b8722e9-76f6-4a0b-b5ae-5ea6f20dc858">
                <l xml:id="m-6aeddf16-e5d5-4c88-bb8e-61b2e5a158a9" facs="#m-96b58b32-d168-46cb-b6d4-c114234abb27" label="text-like">The Solemn afternoon Liturgy</l><l xml:id="m-d5f32289-2fa7-4625-9168-95c7e84e8c72" facs="#m-d5e4b803-0384-4d82-afd4-e03d626888fe" label="ambiguous">747</l><l xml:id="m-9ef5dd14-fd54-4a88-a128-2844196c0810" facs="#m-fa06b161-60eb-4e9b-940b-900d4a789902" label="ambiguous">3 Ant.</l><l xml:id="m-6100869c-9249-4ff6-a3e5-310c5f444f5a" facs="#m-97218bd0-e646-45c9-b11e-6e00c12d7ee7" label="ambiguous">S</l><l xml:id="m-a8f5d00f-3638-41d3-9ae8-50e974442b57" facs="#m-7d39b2db-3ff7-42a4-b5d2-9dd5e2e72bcb" label="lyrics-like">Alvá-tor múndi, sálva nos:</l><l xml:id="m-b5bdc24d-7b37-41e2-bce1-d42e257ed9f8" facs="#m-41d678ca-736b-44b7-87a3-15bdba0fa458" label="lyrics-like">qui per Crúcem et</l><l xml:id="m-b7eecef8-ab22-4dc2-a3d7-248de51403a9" facs="#m-2d004185-dd5f-4c57-bb58-211fc2c2cc68" label="lyrics-like">Sángui-nem rede místi nos,</l><l xml:id="m-e8c5b0d3-edd5-4026-8e4b-5391e057ad3c" facs="#m-8044d10a-6dd8-4d59-a97c-46b73a3bd054" label="lyrics-like">auxi-li-â-re nó-bis, te depre¬</l><l xml:id="m-5e12b157-2d6c-4432-abc6-86ad46df931b" facs="#m-29352a20-8e87-48b8-93c1-fe07e5fcbf72" label="lyrics-like">cámur, Dé-us nóster.</l><l xml:id="m-8d3ec503-79b0-493c-889b-696eb593d2bc" facs="#m-9e01539f-7484-487a-a1db-3483d4522def" label="text-like">25. When they reach the hieh altar, the deacon Ipriestl and the acolvtes</l><l xml:id="m-ef817c27-5011-4fc4-8843-f407422b2c84" facs="#m-d59ee76f-f061-438b-b32b-76924e12fcaf" label="text-like">Iserversl go up the steps, and the deacon Ipriestl places the ciborium on the</l><l xml:id="m-9924fbd3-a1da-4d9a-a0a5-2dae0a7966f7" facs="#m-864b9009-c808-4be3-883c-6986f3cce5f7" label="text-like">corporal, while the acolytes [serversl put their candles on the altar. Au</l><l xml:id="m-e639d498-d865-4cdb-bba7-7cae34dee51c" facs="#m-cafb185e-6e11-4b3b-8902-c229da3b1f61" label="text-like">three ihen genuflect, vohile the humeral veil is taken from the deacon by an</l><l xml:id="m-f4e839b2-2e3a-420b-9ef5-b23d3abceffc" facs="#m-eae69ec1-ee4a-4000-9e20-dea7179476f9" label="text-like">acolyte [serverl; then the deacon goes to the Episile side. The acolytes</l><l xml:id="m-6d6e297b-734c-4992-abf6-d8776098bef1" facs="#m-237246ef-a79e-4b35-ac64-581456a3aca1" label="text-like">Iserversl come down on each side and stand on the louest step of the altar.</l><l xml:id="m-119c627f-ccde-47e2-bce5-9e6828fd02c7" facs="#m-5950b4ae-995a-426f-986b-99e69ecd2434" label="text-like">26. The celebrant and the subdeacon come to the altar, genuflect on both</l><l xml:id="m-cd6976f7-1837-462c-8358-ff43bf932bc0" facs="#m-d48be4eb-2452-4deb-926a-27acba022abe" label="lyrics-like">hnees, go up the steps and genuflect woith the deacon. The célebrant then</l><l xml:id="m-369584ea-8f32-42c7-aa01-23d72f4ae8e8" facs="#m-94e6ef33-7366-4f7a-8747-c3e3358e40be" label="text-like">recites in an audible voice (not singine) the prelude to the Our Father:</l><l xml:id="m-ad464dfa-c04d-40c6-a8e1-8926ec139c97" facs="#m-c4e44e95-4ca6-4b6d-b1a3-f779246da205" label="lyrics-like">Orémus. Praecéptis salutáribus móniti¬</l><l xml:id="m-7c1421b8-aead-44a3-bd43-77e71af7d983" facs="#m-9def75f2-2b2b-486b-b022-c114e143a81e" label="text-like">But, since the Pater noster is the prayer for the Communion, all present,</l><l xml:id="m-be802c8c-951f-4eb8-939f-84a81ee933b0" facs="#m-c12f36d0-e02e-480d-8450-87f86e1a7c49" label="text-like">clergy, servers and people, standine, recite it in Latin with the celebrant,</l><l xml:id="m-c61efc99-bf40-495d-b2be-02a26e9cb12a" facs="#m-ed036045-0888-46cc-b0c8-34a2417ea8bd" label="text-like">gravely and distinctly; and all add Amen at the end.</l><l xml:id="m-8ba3fd9c-6cba-41aa-b0f5-fcc0a1ea00d0" facs="#m-16043671-ed69-4d44-a011-e99e829050e5" label="text-like">The celebrant, with hands joined, alone:</l><l xml:id="m-cb257f0c-2bf6-4586-ba05-9cc9c3bb9bbd" facs="#m-82cb4977-64db-42c3-937b-2d8c4ef44790" label="lyrics-like">Orémus. Praecéptis salutáribus móniti, et divina institutióne</l><l xml:id="m-e5027e99-5838-4de1-84cf-386b02bafd63" facs="#m-cce30003-d8ab-47bd-aac0-7ed6377e443e" label="lyrics-like">formáti, audémus dicere:</l><l xml:id="m-f56e4d16-fe1f-4e38-aa39-f0abec8cc5ed" facs="#m-f807ab5d-2760-4d64-bafa-08db44810a3a" label="text-like">The celebrant heeps his hands joined, and all present continue œith him:</l><l xml:id="m-15a63993-9937-414a-9405-ceb6888552e0" facs="#m-26925230-e628-4b0a-a7db-3850f24570c8" label="ambiguous">PATER NOSTER, QUI ES IN CÆLIS:</l><l xml:id="m-54010f82-a769-4eab-9ac6-6c7aa8042c55" facs="#m-73bdbbca-bce0-42bf-b40c-7f34c73d8620" label="ambiguous">SANCTIFICETUR NOMEN TUUM."</l><l xml:id="m-5ab1999a-4d22-4e0c-9265-b5b8d9c133b0" facs="#m-cab89be5-efb1-417b-8cdb-d3320a0e987d" label="ambiguous">ADVENIAT REGNUM TUUM. "</l><l xml:id="m-50279a4f-a003-4bcc-a154-41787dcc8476" facs="#m-1ad259db-df8f-45d1-9530-508b3eab8497" label="ambiguous">FIAT VOLUNTAS TUA, SICUT IN CÆLO, ET IN TERRA.</l><l xml:id="m-ddf3fc4a-c0b6-4fac-a206-5be367147f7c" facs="#m-728d1dcb-1f87-4fd3-a42b-f1e0d55c2961" label="ambiguous">PANEM NOSTRUM QUOTIDIANUM DA NOBIS HODIE:"</l><l xml:id="m-591a987b-0659-4709-9cee-2298eacdbecd" facs="#m-81512dc2-4410-4831-8fed-eb2ef60e2c36" label="ambiguous">ET DIMITTE NOBIS DEBITA NOSTRA,</l><l xml:id="m-a311b3f0-6ee4-446e-a379-14461647a4d3" facs="#m-17771fed-2b61-4bb5-8ea2-a1017dae6a19" label="ambiguous">SICUT ET NOS DIMITTIMUS DEBITORIBUS NOSTRIS."</l><l xml:id="m-2bbf3f28-d2e8-4c47-a0fe-d07fcfef64e0" facs="#m-198d7b51-cbf7-4355-af54-5624a74ae650" label="ambiguous">ET NE NOS INDUCAS IN TENTATIONEM;"</l><l xml:id="m-2d13a868-eb6d-4fa7-b640-25f1ea5d1bdf" facs="#m-f9b6caba-2533-4b4d-81b7-387d2a434f5d" label="ambiguous">SED LIBERA NOS A MALO."</l><l xml:id="m-eeac82e6-5a53-4050-bde7-c33b6adf7e69" facs="#m-b8195ba0-a28f-41d9-9878-17d13d7c0dfb" label="ambiguous">AMEN.</l><l xml:id="m-2652cf70-87a2-4a7b-91d3-71db6ece8c9d" facs="#m-8d6f0bf2-87d4-4dde-917a-ac53e24b00ac" label="text-like">27. The celebrant alone coutinues, aloud and distinctly, aoith his hand extended:</l><l xml:id="m-e444cf90-1c09-4362-8756-e6ba68f3f7fa" facs="#m-05c56e00-5314-4253-8adf-4dac5434d63d" label="lyrics-like">Ibera nos, quaésumus, Dó-túris: et intercedénte beáta et</l><l xml:id="m-4d051e3a-f02f-4b71-9ad2-035c15963e03" facs="#m-c9caa37d-19cd-4dfd-b7de-35a28e6b8abd" label="lyrics-like">gloriósa semper Virgine Dei Ge¬</l><l xml:id="m-bbb80b86-0a35-42c0-87b4-88ab27160ef3" facs="#m-b0f10e0e-2e25-4043-ad76-bfefc1b56bc6" label="lyrics-like">Al mine, ab ómnibus malis,</l><l xml:id="m-62775834-57fa-45c5-860d-2e6cc18fbd9a" facs="#m-90032aba-a0e4-4c36-bc0b-fb43e65b5769" label="lyrics-like">praetéritis, praeséntibus, et fu- nitrice Maria, cum beátis apó¬</l></lg>
            </div>
          </section>
        </score>
      </mdiv>
    </body>
  </music>
</mei>